--
--   Description
-- 
-- This test verifies that the deference functionality works properly 
-- in the GEM in both normal gigabit mode and burst gigabit mode.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- · Ensures that the GEM defers to carrier sense when the medium 
--     is busy and the GEM has a frame waiting to be sent. (both normal 
--     gigabit mode and burst gigabit mode)
-- · Ensures that carrier extension does not affect the deference process 
--     in normal gigabit mode and burst gigabit mode.
-- · Ensure that the deference statistic is not set when there is a 
--     deference during transmission of a frame and a collision occurs 
--     during transmission of a frame. (both normal gigabit mode and burst 
--     gigabit mode)
--     
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- 
-- Normal Gigabit Mode:
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for gigabit mode.
-- 2. Medium becomes busy (crs is asserted high).
-- 3. Try to transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension. 
--     (Frame should not be transmitted)
-- 4. Medium becomes free. (crs is asserted low).
-- 5. Frame should now transmit completely.
-- 6. Medium becomes busy. (crs is asserted high).
-- 7. Try to transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension. 
--     (Frame should not be transmitted)
-- 8. Medium becomes free. (crs is asserted low).
-- 9. Start to transmit the rest of the minimum sized frame 
--     plus extension. However, collision occurs at the beginning of 
--     carrier extension of the transmitted frame (65th byte).
-- 10. Sometime after the back-off period the minimum sized frame plus 
--      extension should be re-transmitted properly. (deference statistic 
--      should not be set)
-- 11. Medium becomes busy (crs is asserted high)
-- 12. Try to transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension.
--      (Frame should not be transmitted)
-- 13. Medium becomes free (crs is asserted low)
-- 14. Frame transmission starts, but a IFG (late) collision occurs (510th byte)
--      (a late collision interrupt should be received.  A late collision 
--       statistic should be recorded.  No deference statistic should 
--       be recorded)
-- 15. Check status and statistic registers and ensure above operations 
--      were handled properly.
-- 
-- Burst Gigabit Mode:
-- 16. Medium becomes busy (crs is asserted high).
-- 17. In burst mode, try to transmit a minimum sized frame 
--      plus extension. Then, a minimum sized frame. (Frames should 
--      not be transmitted)
-- 18. Medium becomes free. (crs is asserted low).
-- 19. In burst mode, both frames should now transmit completely.
-- 20. Medium becomes busy. (crs is asserted high).
-- 21. In burst mode, try to transmit a minimum sized frame plus 
--      extension. Then, a minimum sized frame. (Frames should not be 
--      transmitted)
-- 22. Medium becomes free. (crs is asserted low).
-- 23. Start to transmit the rest of the minimum sized frame plus 
--      extension. However, collision occurs at the beginning of carrier 
--      extension of the transmitted frame (65th byte). 
-- 24. Sometime after the back-off period the minimum sized frame plus 
--      extension should be re-transmitted properly. Then, the minimum 
--      sized frame should be transmitted properly. (deference statistic 
--      should not be set)
-- 25. Medium becomes busy. (crs is asserted high)
-- 26. In burst mode transmit a minimum length frame with carrier 
--      extension, follwed by a minimum length frame.
-- 27. Medium becomes free. (crs is asserted low)
-- 28. The deferred frames begin transmitting however a collision occurs
--      in the IFG (510th byte).
--      (a late collision interrupt should occur, the mac should drop
--       out of burst mode and the second frame transmitted with 
--       carrier extension - no deference statistic should be recorded)
-- 29. Check status and statistic registers and ensure above operations 
--      were handled properly.
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

